g delay you set, so signing may start later than this. You can choose Refresh to check whether the status has changed.",{at:e}),statusValidating:()=>Apt("Validating"),statusValidatingPopoverHeader:()=>Apt("Validating: stopped signing, still trusted"),statusValidatingPopover:e=>Apt("This certificate has stopped signing, but its chain stays in the trust bundle so certificates already issued under it keep verifying. It becomes inactive at {{at}}. Until then, Enable resumes signing with no wait. You can choose Refresh to check whether the status has changed.",{at:e}),statusInactive:()=>Apt("Inactive"),statusInactivePopoverHeader:()=>Apt("Inactive: retired, no longer trusted"),statusInactivePopover:()=>Apt("This certificate stopped signing and its chain has left the trust bundle, so nothing verifies against it. It stays listed as history until you delete it, and deleting it is safe: no credential depends on it, and the certificate signer keeps signing."),previousCertificates:e=>Apt("Previous certificates ({{certificateCount}})",{certificateCount:e}),previousCertificatesDescription:()=>Apt("Stopped signing and no longer in the trust bundle, so nothing verifies against them. Deleting one is safe."),actionsColumn:()=>Apt("Actions"),verifierSectionTitle:()=>Apt("Certificate verifier information"),trustBundleLabel:()=>Apt("Trust bundle"),trustBundlePopover:()=>Apt("One bundle per provider, and one URL. It carries every authority the provider publishes: both outbound signers, and during an update both the current and incoming certificate authority, which is what lets verifiers accept either one through the handover. Your own AWS agents and workloads get these keys automatically; send this to systems outside AWS."),enabledFlash:e=>Apt(1===e?"Certificate signing enabled. The certificate chain publishes to the trust bundle first, and signing starts in about {{hours}} hour, once every region has it.":"Certificate signing enabled. The certificate chain publishes to the trust bundle first, and signing starts in about {{hours}} hours, once every region has it.",{hours:e}),updatedFlash:e=>Apt(1===e?"Certificate authority updated. The current one keeps signing for about {{hours}} more hour, until the replacement has published everywhere.":"Certificate authority updated. The current one keeps signing for about {{hours}} more hours, until the replacement has published everywhere.",{hours:e}),disabledFlash:()=>Apt("Certificate signer disabled. It stops signing now, its configuration is kept, and Enable resumes signing."),disabledDuringUpdateFlash:()=>Apt("Certificate signer disabled, and the update in progress was stopped with it. Both authorities stay configured, and Enable resumes signing."),resumedFlash:()=>Apt("Certificate signer enabled. Its material was still published, so signing resumed immediately."),resumedInactiveFlash:e=>Apt(1===e?"Certificate signer enabled. Its certificate chain publishes to the trust bundle again first, and signing starts in about {{hours}} hour, after every region has it.":"Certificate signer enabled. Its certificate chain publishes to the trust bundle again first, and signing starts in about {{hours}} hours, after every region has it.",{hours:e}),deletedPublishedFlash:()=>Apt("Certificate deleted. Its chain has been pulled from the trust bundle, so certificates issued under it no longer verify."),deletedInactiveFlash:()=>Apt("Certificate deleted. Its chain had already left the trust bundle, so nothing that was verifying has changed.")},certificateSignerModal:{enableTitle:()=>Apt("Enable certificate signer"),enableDescription:()=>Apt("Issues the X.509-SVIDs this provider's agents and workloads present as client certificates to systems outside AWS. It needs a <link>certificate authority</link> with a subordinate CA in every region you sign in. Standard pricing applies to the creation and use of AWS Private CA."),updateTitle:()=>Apt("Update certificate signer"),updateDescription:()=>Apt("Choose the certificate authority this signer should sign with instead. It needs a <link>certificate authority</link> with a subordinate CA in every region you sign in. The current authority keeps signing until the replacement has been published long enough for verifiers to pick it up."),sourceLabel:()=>Apt("Certificate authority"),sourceUpdateDescription:e=>Apt("Make sure the new certificate authority uses the same algorithm as the current signer, {{algorithm}}. If you choose a different algorithm, you need to disable this signer, delete its certificates, then enable it again with the new authority.",{algorithm:e}),algorithmMismatchOption:(e,t)=>Apt("{{subject}}. Does not match this signer's {{algorithm}} algorithm.",{subject:e,algorithm:t}),algorithmMismatchError:(e,t)=>Apt("This certificate authority uses {{caAlgorithm}}. Rotation keeps the signer's {{signerAlgorithm}} algorithm, so choose a {{signerAlgorithm}} certificate authority instead.",{caAlgorithm:e,signerAlgorithm:t}),sourceThisAccount:()=>Apt("Choose from this account"),sourceOtherAccount:()=>Apt("Use one from another account"),sourceCreateNew:()=>Apt("Create new"),caIdPlaceholder:()=>Apt("Enter the ID of a certificate authority or choose from below"),caIdDescription:()=>Apt("The ID at the end of the certificate authority's ARN in AWS Private CA."),refreshCertificateAuthorities:()=>Apt("Refresh certificate authorities"),loadingCertificateAuthorities:()=>Apt("Loading certificate authorities"),noCertificateAuthorities:()=>Apt("No certificate authorities in this account"),accountIdLabel:()=>Apt("AWS account ID"),accountIdDescription:()=>Apt("The account that owns the certificate authority."),caNameLabel:()=>Apt("Certificate authority name"),caNameDescription:()=>Apt("AWS creates a subordinate CA in every region this provider signs in, and returns an ID for it."),caNameConstraint:()=>Apt("Used as the common name in the certificate authority's subject."),quickCreate:()=>Apt("Quick create"),creatingCa:()=>Apt("Creating certificate authority"),creatingCaInfo:()=>Apt("This usually takes a few minutes. Keep this page open until it finishes."),stepCreatingCa:()=>Apt("Creating the certificate authority"),stepGeneratingKey:()=>Apt("Generating its key"),stepIssuingCaCertificate:()=>Apt("Issuing its CA certificate"),stepActivating:()=>Apt("Activating it"),stepReady:()=>Apt("Ready"),caStillSettingUp:()=>Apt("The certificate authority is still being set up."),caSetupStopped:()=>Apt("Setting up the certificate authority stopped. You can continue from where it left off."),caSetupFailed:()=>Apt("AWS Private CA couldn't set up this certificate authority. Delete it in the AWS Private CA console and try again."),checkAgain:()=>Apt("Check again"),continueSetup:()=>Apt("Continue setup"),caCreated:()=>Apt("Certificate authority created"),quickCreateInfo:()=>Apt("Quick create makes an RSA 2048 certificate authority in AWS Private CA in your account, which has its own charges. The algorithm is fixed and cannot be changed later without setting the signer up again."),managePrivateCas:()=>Apt("Manage CAs and replication in the AWS Private CA console"),owningAccount:()=>Apt("Owning account"),subject:()=>Apt("Subject"),signingDelayLabel:()=>Apt("Minimum signing delay"),signingDelayDescription:()=>Apt("The soonest this certificate can start signing. It publishes to the trust bundle first, so every verifier can check it before anything is signed under it. Signing may start later than this, never sooner."),signingDelayUpdateDescription:()=>Apt("The soonest the new certificate can take over. It publishes to the trust bundle first, so every verifier can check it before anything is signed under it. Signing may start later than this, never sooner."),hours:()=>Apt("hour(s)"),signingDelayConstraint:()=>Apt("1 to 48 hours, in whole hours. Publishing is usually much faster, but can take up to 24 hours."),signingDelayError:()=>Apt("Enter a whole number of hours from 1 to 48."),caIdError:()=>Apt("Enter a certificate authority ID."),accountIdError:()=>Apt("Enter a 12-digit AWS account ID."),caNameError:()=>Apt("Enter a name for the certificate authority."),createCaFirstError:()=>Apt("Create the certificate authority first.")},certificateSignerConfirm:{disableTitle:()=>Apt("Disable certificate signer?"),disableDescription:()=>Apt("This provider stops issuing X.509-SVIDs straight away, and agents and workloads that need a client certificate will start failing on their next request. The certificate below stays configured. Certificates already issued keep verifying for about 12 hours, and Enable resumes signing."),disableDuringUpdateDescription:()=>Apt("This provider stops issuing X.509-SVIDs straight away, and agents and workloads that need a client certificate will start failing on their next request. Both certificates below stop, including the one still in transition, so the update does not complete. Both stay configured. Certificates already issued keep verifying for about 12 hours, and Enable resumes signing."),activeCaId:()=>Apt("Active certificate authority ID"),inTransitionCaId:()=>Apt("In transition certificate authority ID"),resumeTitle:()=>Apt("Enable certificate signer?"),resumeValidatingDescription:()=>Apt("Signing resumes immediately, because this certificate is still published in the trust bundle."),resumeInactiveDescription:e=>Apt(1===e?"This certificate has left the trust bundle, so it publishes again first. Signing starts after about {{hours}} hour, once every region has it.":"This certificate has left the trust bundle, so it publishes again first. Signing starts after about {{hours}} hours, once every region has it.",{hours:e}),deleteTitle:()=>Apt("Delete certificate?"),deletePublishedDescription:()=>Apt("This removes the certificate from the provider and pulls its chain from the trust bundle immediately. The certificate authority itself stays in AWS Private CA, unchanged."),deleteInactiveDescription:()=>Apt("This removes the certificate from the provider. Its chain already left the trust bundle, so nothing that is verifying today changes. The certificate authority itself stays in AWS Private CA, unchanged."),deleteValidatingWarningTitle:()=>Apt("This certificate is validating, so deleting it stops verification immediately"),deleteValidatingWarning:()=>Apt("It has stopped signing, but its chain is still published, so agents and workloads are relying on it to verify credentials issued earlier. Deleting it now pulls the chain at once and those credentials start failing. To avoid this, wait until it becomes inactive on its own. Deleting it then has no effect on verification.")}},Lpt=[".amazonaws.cn",".amazonwebservices.cn"];const Ppt="Actions",Npt="Active",Rpt="Apply",Mpt="Attestation",zpt="Cancel",Opt="Clear",Bpt="Close",Fpt="Configured",$pt="Confirm",jpt="Contains",Wpt="Created",qpt="Delete",Upt="Description",Vpt="Details",Hpt="Disable",Kpt="Dismiss",Gpt="Edit",Ypt="Editing",Jpt="Enable",Zpt="equals",Xpt="Equals",Qpt="Errors",eht="Format",tht="Identifier",aht="Inactive",nht="Info",iht="JWKS",rht="Name",oht="None",sht="Notifications",lht="Operator",cht="Operators",dht="optional",uht="path",pht="Path",hht="Preferences",mht="Preview",ght="Properties",vht="Property",fht="Provided",yht="Provider",bht="Providers",wht="Ready",kht="Recommended",Sht="Refresh",_ht="Remove",xht="Retry",Aht="Save",Eht="scheme",Cht="Scheme",Tht="Scope",Iht="Status",Dht="Subject",Lht="Success",Pht="Tags",Nht="Template",Rht="Templates",Mht="Theme",zht="Today",Oht="Undo",Bht="Update",Fht="Validating",$ht="Value",jht="Values",Wht="Visual",qht="Warning",Uht="Warnings",Vht={"'{{providerName}}' does not exist in your account":"'{{providerName}}' does not exist in your account","(earliest)":"(earliest)","{{addedCount}} tag added or changed":"{{addedCount}} tag added or changed","{{addedCount}} tags added or changed":"{{addedCount}} tags added or changed","{{createdCount}} templates created: {{templateNames}}.":"{{createdCount}} templates created: {{templateNames}}.","{{failed}} of {{total}} certificates could not be deleted, so the provider was not deleted. Resolve the errors, then try again.":"{{failed}} of {{total}} certificates could not be deleted, so the provider was not deleted. Resolve the errors, then try again.","{{failed}} of {{total}} could not be deleted.":"{{failed}} of {{total}} could not be deleted.","{{failed}} of {{total}} templates and identities could not be deleted, so the provider was not deleted. Resolve the errors, then try again.":"{{failed}} of {{total}} templates and identities could not be deleted, so the provider was not deleted. Resolve the errors, then try again.","{{failedCount}} template could not be created. Review the following errors and try again.":"{{failedCount}} template could not be created. Review the following errors and try again.","{{failedCount}} templates could not be created. Review the following errors and try again.":"{{failedCount}} templates could not be created. Review the following errors and try again.","{{identityCount}} identities":"{{identityCount}} identities","{{identityCount}} identity":"{{identityCount}} identity","{{label}} (service mesh)":"{{label}} (service mesh)","{{label}} copied":"{{label}} copied","{{label}} failed to copy":"{{label}} failed to copy","{{label}} template":"{{label}} template","{{label}} template {{index}}":"{{label}} template {{index}}","{{label}}:":"{{label}}:","{{matchCount}} match":"{{matchCount}} match","{{matchCount}} matches":"{{matchCount}} matches","{{name}} has been successfully created.":"{{name}} has been successfully created.","{{name}} has been successfully created. However, the following operations failed:":"{{name}} has been successfully created. However, the following operations failed:","{{providerName}} still has these resources:":"{{providerName}} still has these resources:","{{removedCount}} tag removed":"{{removedCount}} tag removed","{{removedCount}} tags removed":"{{removedCount}} tags removed","{{scope}} · {{domain}}":"{{scope}} · {{domain}}","{{settled}} of {{total}}":"{{settled}} of {{total}}","{{subject}}. Does not match this signer's {{algorithm}} algorithm.":"{{subject}}. Does not match this signer's {{algorithm}} algorithm.","{{tagCount}} tag":"{{tagCount}} tag","{{tagCount}} tags":"{{tagCount}} tags","{{templateCount}} template":"{{templateCount}} template","{{templateCount}} templates":"{{templateCount}} templates","{{templateName}} template failed to create. To try again, <link>add templates</link>. Error details: {{reason}}":"{{templateName}} template failed to create. To try again, <link>add templates</link>. Error details: {{reason}}","{{workload}} fact":"{{workload}} fact","{defined by template}":"{defined by template}","<term>Support:</term> Amazon EKS, Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime, and Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Gateway.":"<term>Support:</term> Amazon EKS, Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime, and Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Gateway.","1 EKS cluster":"1 EKS cluster","1 provider and 1 trust domain per EKS cluster. Each namespace and service account in this cluster gets its own identity, trusted only within this cluster.":"1 provider and 1 trust domain per EKS cluster. Each namespace and service account in this cluster gets its own identity, trusted only within this cluster.","1 to 48 hours, in whole hours. Publishing is usually much faster, but can take up to 24 hours.":"1 to 48 hours, in whole hours. Publishing is usually much faster, but can take up to 24 hours.","1. Select all the check boxes to confirm what deleting {{providerName}} will do.":"1. Select all the check boxes to confirm what deleting {{providerName}} will do.","2. Confirm that you want to delete this provider by typing {{providerName}} below.":"2. Confirm that you want to delete this provider by typing {{providerName}} below.","A declared identity has a fixed name you define. Use one when you need an exact name, for example to match a name another system already expects.":"A declared identity has a fixed name you define. Use one when you need an exact name, for example to match a name another system already expects.","A declared identity has a fixed path you define. Use one when you need an exact path, for example to match a value another system already expects.":"A declared identity has a fixed path you define. Use one when you need an exact path, for example to match a value another system already expects.","A deny, and only for delegated administrators":"A deny, and only for delegated administrators","A fact {{workload}} checks when the agent or workload starts.":"A fact {{workload}} checks when the agent or workload starts.","A fixed label, such as an environment name.":"A fixed label, such as an environment name.","A name to identify this identity.":"A name to identify this identity.","A provider issues secure, verifiable identities to your agents and workloads, like your Kubernetes pods or AI agents, to access AWS and third-party services without long-lived credentials.":"A provider issues secure, verifiable identities to your agents and workloads, like your Kubernetes pods or AI agents, to access AWS and third-party services without long-lived credentials.","A provider with this name already exists.":"A provider with this name already exists.","A tag is a label you assign to an AWS resource. Each tag has a key and an optional value. Use tags to search and filter this provider, or to track your AWS costs.":"A tag is a label you assign to an AWS resource. Each tag has a key and an optional value. Use tags to search and filter this provider, or to track your AWS costs.","A template automatically generates an identity for each matching agent or workload under {{providerName}}.":"A template automatically generates an identity for each matching agent or workload under {{providerName}}.","A template defines the path pattern used to name identities uniquely and the facts an agent or workload must prove before an identity is issued.":"A template defines the path pattern used to name identities uniquely and the facts an agent or workload must prove before an identity is issued.","A template defines the path pattern used to name identities uniquely and the facts an agent or workload must prove before an identity is issued. Decide how this provider issues identities - starting from the <link>default templates</link> for common use cases, or skipping them. Templates are optional and can be added later.":"A template defines the path pattern used to name identities uniquely and the facts an agent or workload must prove before an identity is issued. Decide how this provider issues identities - starting from the <link>default templates</link> for common use cases, or skipping them. Templates are optional and can be added later.","A template names identities automatically as matching agents and workloads start, so you don't create or manage them one by one.":"A template names identities automatically as matching agents and workloads start, so you don't create or manage them one by one.","A template with no attestation policy matches no agent or workload, so nothing is ever issued from it. Set a policy to define which agents and workloads qualify.":"A template with no attestation policy matches no agent or workload, so nothing is ever issued from it. Set a policy to define which agents and workloads qualify.","A template with this name already exists.":"A template with this name already exists.","A template's path pattern, built from facts like cluster, namespace, and service account, names each agent or workload automatically when it starts. You don't create identities ahead of time.":"A template's path pattern, built from facts like cluster, namespace, and service account, names each agent or workload automatically when it starts. You don't create identities ahead of time.","Access a partner API, a SaaS endpoint, or an OIDC service. No setup needed.":"Access a partner API, a SaaS endpoint, or an OIDC service. No setup needed.","Access a service mesh, a database, or an on-premises system.":"Access a service mesh, a database, or an on-premises system.","Access denied":"Access denied","Access you granted to these identities will stop working":"Access you granted to these identities will stop working","Account scoped":"Account scoped",Actions:Ppt,"Activating it":"Activating it",Active:Npt,"Active certificate authority ID":"Active certificate authority ID","Active: currently signing":"Active: currently signing",Add:"Add","Add {{label}} template":"Add {{label}} template","Add a fact or condition key. A path of only custom text would give every agent or workload the same name.":"Add a fact or condition key. A path of only custom text would give every agent or workload the same name.","Add an {{conditionKey}} condition, so only agents or workloads in these clusters get an identity.":"Add an {{conditionKey}} condition, so only agents or workloads in these clusters get an identity.","Add at least 1 path segment.":"Add at least 1 path segment.","Add at least 1 template to continue.":"Add at least 1 template to continue.","Add at least 2 clusters.":"Add at least 2 clusters.","Add attestation policy":"Add attestation policy","Add attestation rules":"Add attestation rules","Add cluster ARN":"Add cluster ARN","Add condition":"Add condition","Add default templates for Amazon EKS, AgentCore Runtime, and AgentCore Gateway.":"Add default templates for Amazon EKS, AgentCore Runtime, and AgentCore Gateway.","Add new tag":"Add new tag","Add policy":"Add policy","Add request-context values like account, Region, or organization.":"Add request-context values like account, Region, or organization.","Add tags":"Add tags","Add tags to this provider for cost management and access control.":"Add tags to this provider for cost management and access control.","Add tags to this template for cost management and access control.":"Add tags to this template for cost management and access control.","Add tags to this workload identity for cost management and access control.":"Add tags to this workload identity for cost management and access control.","Add template":"Add template","Add templates":"Add templates","Add templates after the provider is created.":"Add templates after the provider is created.","Add to the path pattern":"Add to the path pattern","Added or changed tags were not saved":"Added or changed tags were not saved","Adding permissions to govern who can create templates referring to this provider failed. To try again, <link>add policy</link>. Error details: {{reason}}":"Adding permissions to govern who can create templates referring to this provider failed. To try again, <link>add policy</link>. Error details: {{reason}}","Agent and workload identity":"Agent and workload identity","Agent and workload identity - <em>Preview</em>":"Agent and workload identity - <em>Preview</em>","Agent and workload identity in the IAM User Guide":"Agent and workload identity in the IAM User Guide","Agent and workload identity in the IAM User Guide (opens in a new tab)":"Agent and workload identity in the IAM User Guide (opens in a new tab)","Agents and workloads get named automatically":"Agents and workloads get named automatically","Agents and workloads get short-lived credentials that renew automatically and follow the SPIFFE standard, so they work with service meshes such as Istio and with business applications.":"Agents and workloads get short-lived credentials that renew automatically and follow the SPIFFE standard, so they work with service meshes such as Istio and with business applications.","Agents and workloads in these EKS clusters can get an identity from this provider, when all of these are true:":"Agents and workloads in these EKS clusters can get an identity from this provider, when all of these are true:","Agents and workloads running in these clusters can get an identity from this provider. Add two or more.":"Agents and workloads running in these clusters can get an identity from this provider. Add two or more.","Agents and workloads running in this account can use identities generated by this template using information verified by {{workloadLabel}}.":"Agents and workloads running in this account can use identities generated by this template using information verified by {{workloadLabel}}.","Agents and workloads running in this cluster can get an identity from this provider.":"Agents and workloads running in this cluster can get an identity from this provider.","Agents and workloads running in your organization can use identities generated by this template using information verified by {{workloadLabel}}.":"Agents and workloads running in your organization can use identities generated by this template using information verified by {{workloadLabel}}.","Agents and workloads using these identities will stop being issued credentials, and fail on their next request":"Agents and workloads using these identities will stop being issued credentials, and fail on their next request","Agents and workloads, such as AI agents and pods, are verified at runtime and each gets its own identity, generated by a template. The identity gets fine-grained access to AWS resources through IAM policies and CloudTrail, and signed JWT and X.509 credentials for meshes and apps.":"Agents and workloads, such as AI agents and pods, are verified at runtime and each gets its own identity, generated by a template. The identity gets fine-grained access to AWS resources through IAM policies and CloudTrail, and signed JWT and X.509 credentials for meshes and apps.","All outbound signers under this provider will be deleted":"All outbound signers under this provider will be deleted","All properties":"All properties","All templates and identities under this provider will be deleted":"All templates and identities under this provider will be deleted","Allow member accounts to add their own templates, namespaced by account ID":"Allow member accounts to add their own templates, namespaced by account ID","An AI agent or workload gets an identity that is unique.":"An AI agent or workload gets an identity that is unique.","An identity with no attestation policy admits no workload, so nothing can run as it. Set a policy to define which workload qualifies.":"An identity with no attestation policy admits no workload, so nothing can run as it. Set a policy to define which workload qualifies.","An identity with this name already exists.":"An identity with this name already exists.",and:"and","Any value":"Any value",Apply:Rpt,ARN:"ARN","ARN copied":"ARN copied","arn:aws:eks:{Region}:{account ID}:cluster/{cluster name}":"arn:aws:eks:{Region}:{account ID}:cluster/{cluster name}","At runtime the platform attests these facts about the agent or workload. Any agent or workload whose attestation carries them gets an identity issued from this template.":"At runtime the platform attests these facts about the agent or workload. Any agent or workload whose attestation carries them gets an identity issued from this template.",Attestation:Mpt,"Attestation policy":"Attestation policy","Attestation policy for {{name}} has been removed.":"Attestation policy for {{name}} has been removed.","Attestation policy for {{name}} has been updated.":"Attestation policy for {{name}} has been updated.","Auto generated identity name":"Auto generated identity name","Automatically generate from a template":"Automatically generate from a template","Available to every account in your organization ({{organizationId}})":"Available to every account in your organization ({{organizationId}})","Available to this account ({{accountId}})":"Available to this account ({{accountId}})","AWS account ID":"AWS account ID","AWS creates a subordinate CA in every region this provider signs in, and returns an ID for it.":"AWS creates a subordinate CA in every region this provider signs in, and returns an ID for it.","AWS Private CA couldn't set up this certificate authority. Delete it in the AWS Private CA console and try again.":"AWS Private CA couldn't set up this certificate authority. Delete it in the AWS Private CA console and try again.","By continuing, you also enable organization level resource creation, which is needed to create the organization scoped provider. You can disable it later in Settings.":"By continuing, you also enable organization level resource creation, which is needed to create the organization scoped provider. You can disable it later in Settings.","By default, each account's templates require an account ID path prefix to avoid name collisions. You can customize this after creating the provider, under provider settings.":"By default, each account's templates require an account ID path prefix to avoid name collisions. You can customize this after creating the provider, under provider settings.","Can't be changed after the provider is created.":"Can't be changed after the provider is created.","Can't be changed later.":"Can't be changed later.",Cancel:zpt,"Cannot be changed later.":"Cannot be changed later.","Cannot start with aws:":"Cannot start with aws:","Certificate {{name}} (account {{accountId}}): {{reason}}":"Certificate {{name}} (account {{accountId}}): {{reason}}","Certificate authority":"Certificate authority","Certificate authority created":"Certificate authority created","Certificate authority ID":"Certificate authority ID","Certificate authority name":"Certificate authority name","Certificate authority updated. The current one keeps signing for about {{hours}} more hour, until the replacement has published everywhere.":"Certificate authority updated. The current one keeps signing for about {{hours}} more hour, until the replacement has published everywhere.","Certificate authority updated. The current one keeps signing for about {{hours}} more hours, until the replacement has published everywhere.":"Certificate authority updated. The current one keeps signing for about {{hours}} more hours, until the replacement has published everywhere.","Certificate de