ications:sht,"Once the attestation policy is removed, matching agents and workloads will not be issued agent and workload identities until you add a policy again.":"Once the attestation policy is removed, matching agents and workloads will not be issued agent and workload identities until you add a policy again.","One bundle per provider, and one URL. It carries every authority the provider publishes: both outbound signers, and during an update both the current and incoming certificate authority, which is what lets verifiers accept either one through the handover. Your own AWS agents and workloads get these keys automatically; send this to systems outside AWS.":"One bundle per provider, and one URL. It carries every authority the provider publishes: both outbound signers, and during an update both the current and incoming certificate authority, which is what lets verifiers accept either one through the handover. Your own AWS agents and workloads get these keys automatically; send this to systems outside AWS.","One provider and one trust domain shared by every EKS cluster in the mesh. An agent or workload with the same namespace and service account in any of these clusters shares one identity.":"One provider and one trust domain shared by every EKS cluster in the mesh. An agent or workload with the same namespace and service account in any of these clusters shares one identity.","Only the management account or a delegated administrator can delete organization-level providers.":"Only the management account or a delegated administrator can delete organization-level providers.","Only the management account or a delegated administrator can delete organization-level templates.":"Only the management account or a delegated administrator can delete organization-level templates.","Only the management account or a delegated administrator can delete organization-level workload identities.":"Only the management account or a delegated administrator can delete organization-level w