ties to your agents and workloads, like your Kubernetes pods or AI agents, to access AWS and third-party services without long-lived credentials.":"banana","A provider with this name already exists.":"banana","A tag is a label you assign to an AWS resource. Each tag has a key and an optional value. Use tags to search and filter this provider, or to track your AWS costs.":"banana","A template automatically generates an identity for each matching agent or workload under {{providerName}}.":"banana","A template defines the path pattern used to name identities uniquely and the facts an agent or workload must prove before an identity is issued.":"banana","A template defines the path pattern used to name identities uniquely and the facts an agent or workload must prove before an identity is issued. Decide how this provider issues identities - starting from the <link>default templates</link> for common use cases, or skipping them. Templates are optional and can be added later.":"banana","A template names identities automatically as matching agents and workloads start, so you don't create or manage them one by one.":"banana","A template with no attestation policy matches no agent or workload, so nothing is ever issued from it. Set a policy to define which agents and workloads qualify.":"banana","A template with this name already exists.":"banana","A template's path pattern, built from facts like cluster, namespace, and service account, names each agent or workload automatically when it starts. You don't create identities ahead of time.":"banana","Access a partner API, a SaaS endpoint, or an OIDC service. No setup needed.":"banana","Access a service mesh, a database, or an on-premises system.":"banana","Access denied":"banana","Access you granted to these identities will stop working":"banana","Account scoped":"banana",Actions:PCt,"Activating it":"banana",Active:NCt,"Active certificate authority ID":"banana","Active: currently signing":"banana",Add:RCt,"Add {{label}} template