ess.":"banana","Template name values":"banana","Template: {{name}}":"banana",Templates:$Tt,"Templates ({{total}})":"banana","Templates are being created. Wait for the request to finish.":"banana","Templates give matching agents and workloads their own identity name automatically. Each one uses this provider's name prefix, plus a path and pattern.":"banana","Templates that member accounts created under this provider are not visible here and cannot be deleted from this account. If any exist, deleting the provider fails.":"banana","Templates: {{reason}}":"banana","The account that owns the certificate authority.":"banana","The attestation policy controls how identities are issued by this provider. An agent or workload must meet every condition, such as its type, details, and where it runs, as vouched for by the service that hosts it.":"banana","The attestation policy controls how identities are issued by this provider. An agent or workload must meet every condition, such as its type, details, and where it runs, as vouched for by the service that hosts it. Can be edited later.":"banana","The attestation policy controls how identities are issued by this provider. An agent or workload must meet every condition, such as its type, details, and where it runs, as vouched for by the service that hosts it. Generated from the EKS clusters above. Can be edited later.":"banana","The attestation policy controls how this identity is issued. A workload must meet every condition, such as its type, details, and where it runs, as vouched for by the service that hosts it. Can be edited later.":"banana","The attestation policy is the set of facts an agent or workload must prove before this provider issues it an identity. The compute platform vouches for them, so an agent or workload can't claim an identity that isn't its own.":"banana","The attester vouches for the workload, and it must match every condition to run as this identity.":"banana","The certificate authority is still being set up.":"banana","The certificate chain is distributing to every Region, so every verifier can check it before anything is signed under it. It starts signing at {{at}}. That is the minimum signing delay you set, so signing may start later than this. You can choose Refresh to check whether the status has changed.":"banana","The ID at the end of the certificate authority's ARN in AWS Private CA.":"banana","The identity name is the provider's naming scheme, a path prefix, and a path pattern.":"banana","The maximum number of characters you can use in a tag key is 128.":"banana","The maximum number of characters you can use in a tag value is 256.":"banana","The path can be up to {{maxLength}} characters.":"banana","The path doesn't support these segments: {{segments}}. Remove them, and add what you need from the following cards.":"banana","The path is already the default.":"banana","The path is the unique part of each identity's name. Keep the Account ID and Region in front so names stay unique across accounts and Regions, or rearrange the segments to match your team's naming convention.":"banana","The path is the unique part of each identity's name. Keep the Region in front so names stay unique across Regions, or rearrange the segments to match your team's naming convention.":"banana","The path prefixes your policy allows":"banana","The permissions defined in this policy for <b>{{providerName}}</b> stop applying.":"banana","The provider could not be deleted. Try again.":"banana","The provider is being created. Wait for the request to finish.":"banana","The provider might still be deleted. Check the providers list later.":"banana","The resource policy on this provider controls who can associate templates with it.":"banana","The soonest the new certificate can take over. It publishes to the trust bundle first, so every verifier can check it before anything is signed under it. Signing may start later than this, never sooner.":"banana","The soonest this certificate can start signing. It publishes to the trust bundle first, so every verifier can check it before anything is signed under it. Signing may start later than this, never sooner.":"banana",Theme:jTt,"There was an error loading the code editor.":"banana","These clusters set the template's <policyLink>attestation policy</policyLink>.":"banana","These resources need to be deleted before deleting the provider.":"banana","This account ({{accountId}})":"banana","This action deletes the agent and workload identity provider <b>{{providerName}}</b>.":"banana","This cannot be undone, and creating a provider with the same name later does not restore anything. To proceed, complete the steps below.":"banana","This cannot be undone, and the path this template reserved stays reserved. No future template can generate identities under it.":"banana","This cannot be undone, and this name stays reserved. It is never issued again, so you cannot recreate this identity under the same name.":"banana","This certificate authority uses {{caAlgorithm}}. Rotation keeps the signer's {{signerAlgorithm}} algorithm, so choose a {{signerAlgorithm}} certificate authority instead.":"banana","This certificate has left the trust bundle, so it publishes again first. Signing starts after about {{hours}} hour, once every region has it.":"banana","This certificate has left the trust bundle, so it publishes again first. Signing starts after about {{hours}} hours, once every region has it.":"banana","This certificate has stopped signing, but its chain stays in the trust bundle so certificates already issued under it keep verifying. It becomes inactive at {{at}}. Until then, Enable resumes signing with no wait. You can choose Refresh to check whether the status has changed.":"banana","This certificate is validating, so deleting it stops verification immediately":"banana","This certificate stopped signing and its chain has left the trust bundle, so nothing verifies against it. It stays listed as history until you delete it, a